[b][size=5]Description[/size][/b]
[color=#d4d4d8]With this mod you can analyse your Appraised Talismans to find those you don't need, either because you own them multiple times or a better one or when there is no Weapon Type which can utilize all its Skills (details below). It also features an auto-selection of those Talismans at the Melding Pot![/color]
[color=#d4d4d8][size=3][b]Does NOT include craftable Talismans![/b][/size][/color]

[b][size=5]Main features[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][color=#d4d4d8]view all your Appraised Talismans including how many you own[/color][/*]
[*][color=#d4d4d8]view your duplicated Appraised Talismans and how many times you own each[/color][/*]
[*]view your obsolete Appraised Talismans including those that are better
[list]
[*]comes with an option to not compare Slots if the Skills are better[/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[*]view your Appraised Talismans with contradicting Skills[/*]
[*]auto-select the Talismans of each category at the Melding Pot, respecting favorites and manual selection[/*]
[/list]

[b][size=5]Definition of obsolete Talismans[/size][/b]
A Talisman is considered obsolete when either:
[list]
[*]another one has the same Skills but at least one Skill is on a higher level
[list]
[*]Slots must be better or equal (can be disabled)[/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[*]another has the same Skills plus an additional one(s)
[list]
[*]Slots must be better or equal (can be disabled)[/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[*]another has the exact same Skills but better Slots[/*]
[/list]
A Talisman has better Slots when either:
[list]
[*]the Talisman has the same Slot(type)s but at least one Slot is on a higher level[/*]
[*]the Talisman has the same Slot(type)s plus an additional one(s)[/*]
[/list]
[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/images/6993/175266303-1779660518.png[/img][/center]

[b][size=5]Definition of contradicting Talismans[/size][/b]
A Talisman is considered contradicting when there is no Weapon type which can utilize all its Skills.
Examples:
[list]
[*][i]Tetrad Shot[/i] only works on Ranged Weapons (Heavy Bowgun, Light Bowgun, Bow) but [i]Razor Sharp[/i] only works on Melee Weapons, this means a Talisman with both Skills cannot be fully utilized unless switching between a Ranged and a Melee Weapon mid-hunt.[/*]
[*][i]Horn Maestro[/i] only affects Hunting Horn but a Hunting Horn is not affected by guarding Skills ([i]Guard[/i], [i]Guard Up[/i], [i]Offensive Guard[/i]). A Talisman with [i]Horn Maestro[/i] and (at least) one of the guarding Skills is considered contradicting.[/*]
[/list]
[b][color=#ffff00]ATTENTION: The DLC might change Skill compatibilities on some Weapons![/color][/b]
I tried my best to adapt this feature based on the Boosted Action Breakdown videos but those are just guesses! For example: A Talisman with [i]Rapid Fire Up[/i] and [i]Airborne[/i] is no longer considered contradicting.

[b][size=5]Usage[/size][/b]
[list=1]
[*]click on "Analyse Talismans"[/*]
[*]click on either "Show Duplicated Talismans", "Show Obsolete Talismans" or "Show Contradicting Talismans" [/*]
[*]in Melding Pot menu click on "Select for Melding" to auto-select them[/*]
[*][color=#cc0000][b]double check if you really want to meld those Talismans! [/b][/color][/*]
[*]meld the selected Talismans with the in-game "Meld" button[/*]
[/list]
[center][img width=822]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/6993/images/4472/4472-1791567839-569761782.png[/img][/center]

[b][size=5]Known issues[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Should the auto-select feature report an error simply click "Select for Melding" again. Almost ever time it can be ignored and the Talisman was selected after all.[/*]
[*]After using the auto-select feature the in-game "Glowing Stone" counter and the "Required Melding Points" counter is mostly inaccurate. [b]But the confirmation windows are accurate![/b] When the confirmation window asks to "discard x surplus points", you actually have x/10 surplus Melding Points! And when it wants to "use these materials to meld y item(s)" you will get y item(s)![/*]
[/list]
[center][b][img width=812]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/6993/images/4472/4472-1791568103-1782110478.png[/img][/b]
[left][list]
[*]There is a rare bug of the auto-selection feature trying to start the melding process on its own, most of the time without a single Talisman being selected/sufficient melding points. In that case "Cancel" the confirmation and/or press "No" until the confirmation window goes away. Then you can continue.[/*]
[/list]
[center][img width=814]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/6993/images/4472/4472-1791568844-1926534507.png[/img][/center]
[/left]
[/center]

[b][size=5]Installation instructions[/size][/b]
use Fluffy Mod Manager

